-- title:
--   Chart rings of X₁(Mℓ p) as a pushout
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, and a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$; let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A\to L$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid Mp$. Consider four intermediate fields of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, namely $K_M$, $K_N$, $K$, $K'$, pinned to be the $L$-subfields generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of Laurent series, of the $q$-expansion function fields of $\Gamma_1$ of levels $M$, $M\ell$, $Mp$ and $M\ell p$ respectively, each an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L$, and in each of them an element $j_M, j_N, j, j'$, nonzero and equal as a Laurent series to the image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of $j$; assume the inclusions $K_M\le K_N$, $K\le K'$, $K_M\le K$, $K_N\le K'$. For a field $F$ over $A$ and $0 \neq j\in F$, `chartAlgFin A F j` denotes the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $A[j]$. Given $A$-algebra maps $\iota_M$, $\rho$, $\rho'$, $\iota$ between the four such chart rings of $(K_M,j_M)$, $(K_N,j_N)$, $(K,j)$, $(K',j')$, each preserving the underlying Laurent series, and commuting in the sense $\iota(\rho(r))=\rho'(\iota_M(r))$ for all $r$, the conclusion is that, with the algebra structures and scalar towers induced by these maps, the resulting square is a pushout of commutative rings in the sense of `Algebra.IsPushout`: the canonical map $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}(K,j)\otimes_{\mathrm{chartAlgFin}(K_M,j_M)}\mathrm{chartAlgFin}(K_N,j_N)\to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}(K',j')$ is bijective.
--
--   This identifies the $j$-finite integral chart ring of the level $M\ell p$ modular curve with the tensor product of those of levels $Mp$ and $M\ell$ over level $M$, so that properties of the level-raising map at level prime to $p$ (finiteness and étaleness) propagate by base change to level divisible by $p$. It is used in the step establishing étaleness of the level-raising morphism away from the supersingular locus on the two-chart integral model of $X_1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_isPushout_chartAlgFin_levelRaise_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul.lean

